WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.083
Runtime choice affects supported model formats, acceleration backends, memory management, and tuning controls.

00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:07.132
Llama.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:11.956
cpp offers broad portability and direct control over quantized models.

00:00:11.956 --> 00:00:15.941
Ollama provides a convenient model and service workflow.

00:00:15.941 --> 00:00:22.863
LM Studio combines model discovery, local chat, configuration, and API serving in a desktop interface.

00:00:22.863 --> 00:00:27.268
These options are effective for individual and small-team workloads.

00:00:27.268 --> 00:00:37.546
VLLM targets high-throughput serving on supported hardware and can benefit concurrent workloads, but its strengths may not matter for one local interactive user.

00:00:37.546 --> 00:00:48.244
Open WebUI is a front end rather than the inference engine; its responsiveness depends on the backend, network path, and model server beneath it.

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:54.746
Additional layers are worthwhile only when they solve a real interface or operations requirement.

00:00:54.746 --> 00:00:59.151
Match the model format and quantization to the runtime.

00:00:59.151 --> 00:01:05.234
A model optimized for one loader may be unsupported or inefficient in another.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:11.317
Driver versions, acceleration libraries, runtime builds, and hardware architecture form a compatibility chain.

00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:15.302
Track known-good versions and verify acceleration after changes.

00:01:15.302 --> 00:01:22.224
Newer software may improve performance, but it may also change defaults, memory use, or stability.

00:01:22.224 --> 00:01:28.307
Choose the simplest runtime that provides the required model support, control, and interface.

00:01:28.307 --> 00:01:37.327
Benchmark candidates with the same model and workload, then include setup time, reliability, logs, updates, and recovery in the decision.

00:01:37.327 --> 00:01:47.605
A stable runtime that starts predictably and produces repeatable results is often better than a more complex stack with a small peak-speed advantage.
